    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#1",
      "line": 207,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Execution.lean",
      "rule": "R11",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The new DROP COLUMN branch has no executable regression test, and its conditional preservation proofs can pass even if the acceptance guard always rejects. Fix: add concrete tests for an accepted drop, preserved cells and rowids, and rejection with an unchanged database."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#2",
      "line": 40,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ColumnDropCatalog.lean",
      "rule": "R7",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The blanket rejection of referenced parent tables is not identified as a model restriction, although SQLite permits dropping their unreferenced columns. Fix: distinguish this model restriction from the SQLite dependency rules in the guard's documentation."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#3",
      "line": 18,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/DropColumnDatabaseLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The plain-words statement of `rows_modify_getD` omits the assumption that `change [] = []`, which matters for absent positions. Fix: state that the transformation must preserve the empty list."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#4",
      "line": 27,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/DropColumnLinkLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The docstrings of `childValues_mapChildren` and `ForeignKeyLink.satisfied_mapChildren` omit their selected-position membership assumptions, and the former also omits the relationship between the links' child columns. Fix: restate these premises explicitly in each theorem's docstring."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#5",
      "line": 64,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ColumnDropParentLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The docstrings of `CatalogObject.isTrigger_dropColumn` and `Catalog.find_mapIdx` describe preservation of object kinds, but their formulas only preserve whether an object is a trigger. Fix: describe the trigger predicate precisely and state that the formulas do not distinguish the other kinds."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#6",
      "line": 96,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/PreservationLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The updated `step_extends` excludes DROP COLUMN through `kind ≠ .rewrite`, but its plain-words statement still names only DROP and RENAME as excluded operations. Fix: add DROP COLUMN to the stated exclusions."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#7",
      "line": 25,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ColumnDropExprLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The new expression theorem docstrings use unchecked `{lit}` references for declarations such as `EvalContext.RowFree`, `Expr.readsColumn` and `Expr.dropColumn`. Fix: use checked `{name}` references for declaration names in these proposition statements."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#8",
      "line": 47,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ColumnDropParentLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R3",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "`Identifier.sameName_comm`, `CatalogObject.name_dropColumn` and `CatalogObject.isTrigger_dropColumn` are used by other proofs but have no proof sketches. Fix: add a short strategy sentence to each docstring."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261027T074345Z-1230d27d#9",
      "line": 15,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/DropColumnReferenceLaws.lean",
      "rule": "R3",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "`ForeignKey.mapColumns_id` is used by the subsequent transport proof but has no proof sketch. Fix: explain that unfolding the mapping reduces the result to the identity map."
